WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.330
In the midst of some of the worst civil unrest
that we've seen in this country for a long

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:11.679
time, coming at the juncture of a 100 year
pandemic, police killings of black men that

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:16.400
have generated massive protests, a huge economic
recession.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:23.470
Donald Trump is now bragging he has been the
best president for black people since Abraham

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.840
Lincoln.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:30.160
Trump tweeting this week, quote, My administration
has done more for the black community than

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:36.050
any president since Abraham Lincoln passed
opportunity zones, which, with Senator Tim

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:43.850
Scott, guaranteed funding for HBC use, school
choice, past criminal justice reform, lowest

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:49.560
black unemployment, poverty and crime rates
in history, and then adding in a second tweet

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.170
in all caps.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.530
And the best is yet to come.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.720
So let's pretend that this is serious and
this is a serious person making a serious

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.720
claim.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.620
The first question is, does this even pass
the sniff test?

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:06.950
Does it pass the test that Tump Trump has
done more for the black community than any

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.420
president taking all the way back to Abraham
Lincoln?

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.400
It doesn't sound right and obviously it's
not right.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.050
And Trump's persistent dog whistles to white
nationalists are only a tiny, tiny piece of

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.050
it.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.960
But let's pick one of those things and actually
think about it in a little bit more detail.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:29.620
So one of the claims that Trump regularly
made before 25 percent of the workforce lost

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:35.930
their jobs because a corona virus was that
black unemployment is at record lows and that

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.380
Trump is, of course, to thank for that.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.260
A couple of things.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:46.909
What you need to understand is that when unemployment
is very low, it's typically low for every

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:47.909
group.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:53.510
So we no doubt had a very low unemployment
rate up until the Corona virus pandemic started

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.180
when we talked about the economy leading up
to the pandemic.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.940
I made no effort to deceive or hide the fact
that we had a low unemployment rate.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.950
It was very low for white people.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.229
It was low for black people.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:07.490
It was, you know, low for young and old people.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.229
It was low for men and women.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.160
It was low for college graduates, a non college
graduate.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:17.639
So thinking back to my interview earlier this
week with Jonathan Faber about critical thinking,

00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:22.519
was black unemployment low because of something
Trump did?

00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:29.670
Was black unemployment low and it applied
to all groups because of something Trump did?

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.200
Or was this part of the sort of natural cycle
of the economy?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:39.739
What we know is job growth certainly slowed
from the pace under Barack Obama.

00:02:39.739 --> 00:02:43.510
But again, only some of this has to do with
the president.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:51.029
So the logical question to ask would be what
specifically did Donald Trump do that disproportionately

00:02:51.029 --> 00:02:58.140
created jobs for black Americans relative
to nonblack Americans?

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.989
And when you actually boil it down and think
about it in this way, Trump didn't do anything.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:02.989
There was nothing.

00:03:02.989 --> 00:03:04.769
Now, I'm gonna give you one other example
of this.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:11.829
Remember, during Barack Obama's presidency,
the right would regularly say a record number

00:03:11.829 --> 00:03:14.329
of people aren't working.

00:03:14.329 --> 00:03:18.810
A record number of people are outside of the
labor force.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:23.769
And then Trump is inaugurated and instantly,
up until three months ago.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:30.879
Some of those same people were saying a record
number of people are working now.

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:31.920
And it didn't sound right.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:37.510
How is it that we went from record numbers
of people not working under Obama to record

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:39.849
numbers of people working under Donald Trump?

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:40.849
Doesn't really make sense.

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:46.150
Well, the truth is, during Obama's presidency,
a record number of people were working and

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:49.029
a record number of people were not working.

00:03:49.029 --> 00:03:53.499
Likewise, during Trump's presidency, before
coronavirus, of course, a record number of

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.700
people were working and a record number of
people were not working.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.110
How is this possible?

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:00.299
The answer is the population keeps growing.

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:06.569
If at any given time, roughly 55 percent of
the population is in the workforce and 45

00:04:06.569 --> 00:04:08.909
percent of the population is out of the workforce.

00:04:08.909 --> 00:04:13.999
As long as our population keeps growing, you
will simultaneously continue to have more

00:04:13.999 --> 00:04:18.169
people working than ever before and more people
not working than ever before.

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:20.100
The devil is in the details.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.030
Why are people not working?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.280
Is it because they don't have to?

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.960
Because the economy's doing really well?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.960
Is it because there are no jobs?

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.039
Is it because there's been a population shift
to more older folks who are retirement age

00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:35.979
or a population shift to a lot of more college
aged people who, when they are not working,

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:39.849
even if you're in college full time, you count
as being out of the labor force.

00:04:39.849 --> 00:04:41.500
How much are people earning?

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.680
Are their wages allowing them to afford the
cost of living wherever it is that they live?

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.650
So as you can very quickly see, for a long
time we've had a record number of people working

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.850
and a record number of people not working
coronavirus.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.949
Of course, this has changed that.

00:04:54.949 --> 00:04:59.250
But the question is, is Trump doing more for
black?

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.030
People than anyone since Abraham Lincoln.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:06.939
That is obviously untrue, and it's something
that only a pathological, pathological liar

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:09.949
or completely delusional person would say.

00:05:09.949 --> 00:05:11.850
They lie for the sake of lying.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.940
They are hyperbolic in their lies.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:15.449
And that's all that this is.

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:15.771
And let's not be confused about it.

